## Published Research and Prior Art

This section records published research that informed independently implemented algorithms or architectural decisions.

Citing a publication does not imply that its software, datasets, or pretrained weights are included in this repository.

### Grasping and Suction

Dex-Net 3.0
Mahler et al., ICRA 2018

The analytic vacuum and wrench model implemented in `src/robot/grasping/suction/wrench.py` is based on the statics described in the publication.

SuctionNet-1Billion
Cao et al., RA-L 2021

Sim-Suction

The deformable-cup seal formulation implemented in `src/robot/grasping/suction/seal.py` is based on the published formulation.

No source code, dataset, or pretrained checkpoint from these projects is included in or required by this repository.

The GraspNet-1Billion dataset and pretrained weights are subject to non-commercial licensing terms and are not used, fetched, or redistributed by this repository.

### Learned Grasp Generator

The learned grasp generator in `src/robot/grasping/deep/` was developed with reference to published work in point-cloud-based 6-DoF grasp detection.

Relevant publications include:

GraspNet-1Billion and graspness-based detection
Fang et al., CVPR 2020
Wang et al., ICCV 2021

Volumetric Grasping Network
Breyer et al., CoRL 2020

Implicit-feature successor
Jiang et al., RSS 2021

The implementation is based on the published descriptions and is independently implemented in this repository. No source code, dataset, or pretrained checkpoint from these projects is included in or required by this repository.

The training data used by this repository is generated from CC0, CC-BY, and self-produced assets.

### PointNetV3

Guocheng Qian, Hasan Abed Al, Guohao Li, Ali Thabet, Bernard Ghanem
*Anisotropic Separable Set Abstraction for Efficient Point Cloud Representation Learning*
NeurIPS 2021
https://openreview.net/forum?id=PMY3C3E7xj

This work was consulted as a reference for the PointNetV3 architecture and its Anisotropic Separable Set Abstraction (ASSA) modules. The implementation in this project was independently developed and does not copy source code from the referenced work.


### Additional Research References

arXiv:2606.00998

The published work informed the use of gripper conditioning as a swept-volume representation. The representation used in this repository is independently implemented and uses a repository-specific parameterization.

arXiv:2410.04826

The published work informed the representation of rotational symmetry using the director representation

M(v) = vvᵀ − I/3

The implementation in this repository is independent.

arXiv:2507.13097

The published work informed the normalization approach used for local point-cloud crops. The numerical values used in this repository were determined independently from measurements on the project's own data.

### Serialized Point-Cloud Processing

Published work on serialized point-cloud processing informed the ordering of point clouds along space-filling curves and the use of windowed attention.

The implementation in `src/robot/grasping/deep/net/serialized.py` is independently implemented. It uses Z-order curves with permuted axes rather than reproducing the exact published implementation.

No source code from the referenced work is included in this repository.

